WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.886
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online C one, Book four.

2
00:00:05.186 --> 00:00:08.665
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.965 --> 00:00:16.528
Unit nineteen: Strategic Leadership. Today you will describe leadership demands with depends on / requires + noun phrase.

4
00:00:16.828 --> 00:00:19.295
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.233 --> 00:00:23.571
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:25.894
Strategic leadership.

7
00:00:26.883 --> 00:00:31.425
Strategic leadership means guiding an organisation toward long-term goals.

8
00:00:32.017 --> 00:00:36.071
Strategic leadership turned the small cooperative into a national brand.

9
00:00:36.683 --> 00:00:39.893
Your turn. Say: Strategic leadership.

10
00:00:42.733 --> 00:00:44.292
Strategic leadership.

11
00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:46.248
Vision alignment.

12
00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:52.106
Vision alignment means ensuring everyone works toward the same long-term goal.

13
00:00:52.717 --> 00:00:55.691
Vision alignment workshops united the three departments.

14
00:00:56.283 --> 00:00:59.121
Your turn. Say: Vision alignment.

15
00:01:01.967 --> 00:01:03.130
Vision alignment.

16
00:01:03.883 --> 00:01:05.720
Organizational agility.

17
00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:11.340
Organizational agility means an organisation's ability to adapt quickly.

18
00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:15.296
Organizational agility helped them survive the pandemic.

19
00:01:15.883 --> 00:01:19.035
Your turn. Say: Organizational agility.

20
00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:23.772
Organizational agility.

21
00:01:24.517 --> 00:01:25.843
Talent development.

22
00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:30.266
Talent development means building employees' skills and potential.

23
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.254
Talent development reduced their reliance on foreign managers.

24
00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:37.665
Your turn. Say: Talent development.

25
00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.873
Talent development.

26
00:01:42.617 --> 00:01:44.001
Succession planning.

27
00:01:45.017 --> 00:01:49.048
Succession planning means preparing future leaders to replace current ones.

28
00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.215
Without succession planning, the family firm struggled after the founder retired.

29
00:01:54.817 --> 00:01:57.968
Your turn. Say: Succession planning.

30
00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:02.438
Succession planning.

31
00:02:03.183 --> 00:02:04.324
Culture building.

32
00:02:05.317 --> 00:02:09.638
Culture building means shaping the shared values and behaviours of an organisation.

33
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.132
Culture building starts with how leaders behave daily.

34
00:02:13.717 --> 00:02:16.915
Your turn. Say: Culture building.

35
00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:20.977
Culture building.

36
00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.020
Decision-making.

37
00:02:24.017 --> 00:02:27.607
Decision-making means the process of choosing between options.

38
00:02:28.217 --> 00:02:31.191
Clear decision-making rules ended endless meetings.

39
00:02:31.783 --> 00:02:35.109
Your turn. Say: Decision-making.

40
00:02:37.967 --> 00:02:40.047
Decision-making.

41
00:02:40.783 --> 00:02:42.272
Long-term thinking.

42
00:02:43.283 --> 00:02:47.233
Long-term thinking means considering consequences many years ahead.

43
00:02:47.850 --> 00:02:51.254
Long-term thinking led them to invest in staff training.

44
00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:55.060
Your turn. Say: Long-term thinking.

45
00:02:57.900 --> 00:03:00.399
Long-term thinking.

46
00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:05.211
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:13.277
Visal, the founder of a successful Cambodian construction firm is retiring, but nobody is ready to replace her. Why?

48
00:03:14.383 --> 00:03:23.560
Because she made every major decision herself. Strategic leadership requires talent development, not just personal brilliance.

49
00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:27.137
But the company grew fast under her control.

50
00:03:28.250 --> 00:03:35.895
It did. However, lasting success depends on succession planning and a culture that survives beyond one person.

51
00:03:36.983 --> 00:03:38.994
What should she do in her final year?

52
00:03:40.083 --> 00:03:50.329
Delegate real authority now. Building future leaders requires patience, trust and a willingness to watch others make mistakes.

53
00:03:51.467 --> 00:03:53.095
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:53.950 --> 00:03:58.167
Grammar focus: Depends on and requires plus noun phrase.

55
00:03:58.467 --> 00:03:59.607
Look at the pattern.

56
00:04:00.317 --> 00:04:03.675
Strategic leadership requires long-term thinking.

57
00:04:04.583 --> 00:04:08.069
Lasting success depends on careful succession planning.

58
00:04:08.983 --> 00:04:11.865
Building future leaders demands patience and trust.

59
00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:24.459
'Require' is followed by a noun phrase or 'object + to-infinitive' (requires staff to adapt), but not directly by a to-infinitive: 'requires long-term thinking', not 'requires to think long-term'.

60
00:04:25.217 --> 00:04:29.936
Be careful! Don't say: Leadership requires to think long-term.

61
00:04:31.900 --> 00:04:35.211
Say: Leadership requires long-term thinking.

62
00:04:35.511 --> 00:04:37.476
Requires + noun phrase.

63
00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.989
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:41.800 --> 00:04:43.312
Leading Beyond Today.

65
00:04:43.612 --> 00:04:51.382
Strategic leadership differs from day-to-day management because it focuses on where an organisation should be in ten years, not ten days.

66
00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:59.103
It requires the ability to interpret trends, align people around a shared vision and make difficult trade-offs.

67
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:06.813
Effective strategic leaders also recognise that an organisation's future depends on talent development and succession planning.

68
00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:14.444
Many family businesses in Southeast Asia have struggled because authority remained concentrated in a single founder.

69
00:05:15.433 --> 00:05:22.715
Ultimately, a leader's success is measured less by what they achieve personally than by what the organisation achieves after they leave.

70
00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:27.813
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:28.650 --> 00:05:30.557
Good leadership requires blank.

72
00:05:30.857 --> 00:05:34.615
A, to listen. B, careful listening. C, listen.

73
00:05:38.167 --> 00:05:40.665
The answer is B: careful listening.

74
00:05:41.817 --> 00:05:44.919
Preparing future leaders to replace current ones is blank.

75
00:05:45.219 --> 00:05:50.057
A, succession planning. B, culture building. C, decision-making.

76
00:05:53.600 --> 00:05:55.901
The answer is A: succession planning.

77
00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.944
Building employees' skills and potential is blank.

78
00:06:00.244 --> 00:06:05.534
A, vision alignment. B, organizational agility. C, talent development.

79
00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:11.843
The answer is C: talent development.

80
00:06:12.983 --> 00:06:14.600
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:06:14.900 --> 00:06:22.315
A, The role requires to travel often.. B, The role requires frequent travel.. C, The role requires of travel..

82
00:06:25.867 --> 00:06:29.190
The answer is B: The role requires frequent travel..

83
00:06:30.350 --> 00:06:33.812
According to the reading, a leader's success is measured by…

84
00:06:34.112 --> 00:06:40.633
A, personal wealth. B, what the organisation achieves after they leave. C, the number of meetings.

85
00:06:44.200 --> 00:06:48.115
The answer is B: what the organisation achieves after they leave.

86
00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:52.138
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:52.983 --> 00:06:56.492
What quality do you think defines truly strategic leadership?

88
00:07:13.283 --> 00:07:14.749
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:07:15.049 --> 00:07:53.976
I think the defining quality of strategic leadership is long-term thinking combined with the humility to develop others. Many managers can solve today's problems, but strategic leadership requires imagining the future and preparing the organisation for it. For example, a leader who invests in training young staff may see lower profits this year but a much stronger company in ten years. Such leadership also depends on clear communication, because a vision is useless unless everyone understands and shares it.

90
00:07:54.276 --> 00:07:56.009
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:56.917 --> 00:08:02.611
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and depends on and requires plus noun phrase.

92
00:08:02.911 --> 00:08:08.280
Today's value is strategic vision. See the bigger picture, and plan for where you want to be.

93
00:08:08.580 --> 00:08:11.046
See you in Unit twenty. Goodbye!

94
00:08:11.346 --> 00:08:15.055
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

